# 1640s heavy horse (2026-10-18): the caracole - trot up to pistol shot, fire, wheel off.
drill "Caracole"
era 1640s
about "The old German way: trot up to pistol shot, fire, wheel off to reload. Charges home only on horse, broken foot, or once the pistols are spent."
type Cuirassier
dials aggression 0.50 discipline 0.80 cohesion 0.80 cover 0.00 patience 0.80 nerve 0.80

sergeant:
  when enemy breaking or enemy broken                    -> charge
  when enemy mounted and enemy within 60                 -> charge; form tight
  when out of ammo and enemy within 80                   -> charge; form tight
  when enemy within 14                                   -> volley; fall back 30
  when enemy within 70                                   -> advance
  otherwise                                              -> advance; hold fire

man:
  when volley called and loaded                          -> fire
  when enemy within 13 and loaded                        -> fire
  when charging                                          -> charge
  otherwise                                              -> follow sergeant
